WEBVTT

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.910
<i>Rice which practically melts in the mouth,</i>

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.960
<i>wrapped in crispy, sweet deep-fried tofu.</i>

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.000
<i>This is the taste of bliss.</i>

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:09.020
<i>Peel the radish piece by piece...</i>

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.900
<i>Slowly, so it doesn't lose its shape.</i>

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.700
<i>Sprinkle salt over the mackerel, and then rinse it with hot water to remove the fishy smell.</i>

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.910
<i>Slowly and steadily,</i>

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:27.460
<i>add a helping of effort and a helping of love,</i>

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.960
<i>and your dish will...</i>

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.920
Not end up tasty at all!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.260
It smells so good, but why does it taste so bad?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:49.100
<i>Grandma... The longer I live alone, the worse of a cook I become...</i>

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.940
Listen, Ryo.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.360
The better a cook you are,
the better a wife you'll make.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.860
<i>Sorry, Grandma!</i>

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.740
<i>If this keeps up...</i>

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.990
I'll be a terrible wife!

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.660
Hello, this is Machiko Ry—

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.330
Akira!

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.630
Sorry I couldn't make it down for New Year's. Work has me buried.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.720
Don't worry about me. I know you're working hard.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.380
Aww, c'mon,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:27.140
what kind of terrible aunt leaves an eighth-grader all alone?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.640
No, really, I'm fine.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.770
I've just accepted the fact that I'm going to be forever alone.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.270
At least it's better than being a terrible wife.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.440
Say what?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.030
Oh, nothing...

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:41.610
Oh yeah, I was gonna ask you something.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.450
Mackerel and radish...

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.410
My second cousin's transferring into the same grade at my cram school?

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.830
Yeah, she also wants to go to
the same art prep school.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.040
Her classes are on Sundays, so d'ya think she can crash at your place on Saturday nights?

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.920
She's trying to get into the same school?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.090
I don't know. I'm really busy studying for exams,

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:07.310
and I wouldn't be able to cook for her or anything.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.100
Don't worry! She'll eat anything as long as you serve it wearing nothing but an apron!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.440
No way!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.480
<i>I ended up agreeing to it.</i>

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.410
I wish I was like that...

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.120
<i>On a cold night like this,</i>

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:34.080
<i>I just want to be in a warm room cooking a warm meal</i>

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.210
<i>for someone who makes my heart warm.</i>

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.000
Who's that?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.340
I can't breathe!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.760
You're Machiko Ryo, right?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.850
Hello. I'm Morino Kirin.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.360
Sure am!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.320
Are you <i>sure</i> you're my age?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.200
N-Never mind!

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.410
Those bags look so heavy.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.200
Did you carry them all by yourself?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.000
Yep. I'm plenty strong.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.500
Oh, by the way, here!

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.670
Napa cabbage?

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:19.170
Yeah, I pinched a few from home.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.800
P-Pinched?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.590
You mean you took them without telling anyone?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.720
Well...

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:31.970
I had a fight with my parents on the way out the door...

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.600
Voilà! Dinner is served!

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.730
I dunno why you expect me to be excited.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.230
I don't hate veggie stir-fry,
but why don't you ever cook meat?

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.360
There's plenty of meat right there!

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.610
The seasoning's sukiyaki-flavored too.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.030
It's great!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.910
Um...

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:52.660
What?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.700
An art school in Tokyo?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.670
Are you saying you want to move to Tokyo?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.420
Yep.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.710
Aren't the exams there totally different?

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.000
Won't you have to go to cram school?

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:03.920
I suppose.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.380
I've already applied to a cram school in Tokyo.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.090
They offer Sunday classes, so—

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.430
Without even asking me?!

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.680
Dear, uh...

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.100
Don't worry about the cost.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.310
I got a scholarship that'll cover tuition—

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.640
That's not the problem!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.940
You are <i>not</i> going to that cram school.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.440
I don't care about your exams.
Tokyo is simply too far away.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.610
Th-Then...

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:33.780
I'm just going to move to Tokyo and live with someone who'll cook tasty meals for me!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.450
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.580
It might've been my fault since I never really mentioned it at all until then.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:45.880
But they ended up saying it was okay if you stayed with me?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.760
Yeah. They think I'll just give up after a while.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.720
Hm? Are you catching a cold?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.810
It's freezing out here, and those
clothes don't look terribly warm.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.980
Well, I'm going to prep school in Tokyo!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.940
None of the girls I see in magazines wear coats!

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.360
I-Is that so?

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.490
I don't care what my mom says.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.740
I'm going to school in Tokyo.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.370
Um...

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.630
Are you hungry?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.930
Um...

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:38.810
<i>Is this some kind of eating contest?</i>

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:43.060
Oh, sorry! It looked so good, I forgot to thank you!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:44.980
Thank you for the food!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.980
It's totally delish!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.660
Really? I'm glad you like it!

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:56.160
I figured a hot soup would be good since you're coming down with a cold and all.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.870
It's wonderful!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.330
It's been ages since I've had anything that's not veggie stir-fry.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.000
Is that so?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Our meals at home are pretty haphazard.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.380
Your cooking's so much better, Ryo!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.380
That's just because you're hungry.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:16.890
They say hunger is the best sauce, right?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.480
I've actually been worried
about my cooking lately...

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.730
You shouldn't be!

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.690
This is the best hot pot I've ever had!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:28.440
This is a once-in-a-lifetime hot pot!

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.990
Here, open up and try some for yourself!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.240
I'm telling you, it's great!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.030
I-I can help myself...

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.870
Open wide, before it gets cold!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.830
B-But...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.040
Sigh...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.710
I'll eat it!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.460
You will?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.380
Say "ah"!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.690
I-It's good.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.070
I-I think you're enjoying it a little <i>too</i> much.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.570
Don't look at me like that!
I can't eat any more if you do...

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.830
You're incredible, Ryo.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.750
We're the same age, but you're so mature,

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.080
and a good cook to boot.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:27.120
Hardly. It's a very simple dish.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.750
I'm sure you could make it too.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.130
Really?

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:30.920
Really!

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.420
So you think I could live alone?

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.140
I mean,

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.640
if I could make a hot pot like this,
then perhaps I could live by myself in Tokyo.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:49.060
Maybe after you learn to eat your carrots.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.820
I-I just can't stand their smell!

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.990
Finish your carrots, and then take some medicine.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:03.540
<i>I'm glad she finished it all.</i>

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.250
<i>That hot pot came out nicely, if I may say so myself.</i>

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.550
<i>I wonder why, though?</i>

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:19.260
<i>It's a simple recipe. It must have been the fresh cabbage she brought.</i>

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.390
<i>Oh, I wonder if I can use the cores for anything?</i>

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:24.720
Coming!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.850
How's Kirin doing?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.650
She's taking a bath right now.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.940
I see.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.990
I was surprised since she asked me out of nowhere.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.410
She asked you herself?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.120
Yeah.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.320
Wrote a letter and everything.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.910
That's pretty old-fashioned.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:50.120
I don't think her mom's as mad about this as she's letting on.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.210
Maybe she's just worried she'll be lonely.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.590
Lonely?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.590
So you think I could live alone?

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.340
You shouldn't stay in the bath
too long when you're sick!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.100
Hello?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.810
37.2 degrees... That's pretty high.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.360
And on my first day of school too...

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:19.150
You should dress warmly.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.280
I'll lend you my coat.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.790
Um...

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.040
It's a bit big, but that's a good thing right now.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:37.880
I don't want the Tokyo girls to think I'm some midget from the sticks.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.670
I don't think the coat's going to make any difference.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:43.390
This is my class.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.890
I think you're on the second floor.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.140
Hey, Machiko!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.600
Good morning.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.850
Who's this? Your little sister?

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:53.980
She's so cute!

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.360
Hi there!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.780
I don't think the length of your skirt makes any difference either.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.410
<i>Kirin's taking a long time.</i>

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.920
<i>I wonder if her cold's getting to her?</i>

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.790
<i>She was running a fever.</i>

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.760
Why, you've got a fever too!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.420
That's all right. Tonight, I'll make you my special...

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.890
How was your day?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.770
That's a ton of books.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:36.310
Cah ya hol' up a tisshew fir meh?

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:36.900
What?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.230
Ahh neeeh ta bloww muh nush.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:43.030
Oh, you need to blow your nose?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.580
I feel like I'm about to pass out...

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.950
Kirin?!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.500
No, don't worry.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.040
Thanks.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.920
Yeah.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.420
I understand.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.170
Talk to you later.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.390
Was that my mom?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:09.970
She was out, so I spoke to your dad.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.850
He was worried.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.060
Oh...

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.890
So was your mom.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.400
He asked if you could stay another night.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.950
Even if it's just a cold, it's not good to go on a long train ride while you're not feeling well.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.700
Thanks.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.160
Anyway, are you hungry?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.080
I thought I'd make udon for tonight
since it's nice and easy on the stomach.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:36.500
That sounds great! I could use some
instant kitsune udon right about now!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.460
You're fine with something so simple?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.960
I love the crispy, crunchy deep-fried tofu!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.130
How about I make the real thing?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.630
You know how to?!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.180
It's simple.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.510
All you need is soy sauce, cooking wine,
sugar, and a bit of water.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.270
That's amazing!

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:56.060
You could probably drive the instant cup stuff belly-up!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.690
That was a compliment, right?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.520
Here you go, homemade kitsune udon.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:06.700
I pickled the cabbage cores from yesterday too.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.070
Thank you so much!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.380
Super delish!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:24.670
The slippery noodles, fried tofu,
and broth are all great together!

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.920
The leek is nice and sweet too!

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:31.850
Grandma always made it for me when I had a cold.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:37.060
I wish I could make things like this!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:40.400
Ooh, I feel warm all over!

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.650
I added a bit of ginger.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.980
Ginger warms you up.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.570
I made plum tea too.
It'll help bring your fever down.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.580
Do you want to be a doctor someday, Ryo?

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.120
All I did was make some udon...

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.000
All right, now take your medicine and go to bed.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.460
Aren't you going to have dinner?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.840
Oh, I'm fine with whatever.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.550
Hi, I'd like to order a pizza.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.590
Yeah, the usual toppings.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.260
There we go.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.350
And time to eat.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.020
Inari sushi!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.060
Oh, this is just, uh...

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:29.240
I ran out of udon, so I took the leftover tofu and...

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:31.490
No fair! Leave some for me!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.660
No! Eating too much is bad for your stomach.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.660
Save it for when you're better.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.250
<i>She's like me when I was little.</i>

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.550
Gimme! Gimme!
<i>She's like me when I was little.</i>

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.720
What are you grinning about?! Hmph!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.470
It's nothing!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.810
Anyway, let's eat.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.230
The sweet, deep-fried tofu is incredible!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.110
And the rice inside is so fluffy!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.530
Put together, it's such a juicy combination!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.160
I can't eat like this!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.330
The rice is seasoned perfectly too!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.710
And it's all wrapped so well!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.460
Come on!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:32.220
Ryo, you know everything!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.840
I'm just doing what Grandma did for me.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:40.520
I see. So that's how family recipes get passed down!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:45.900
Yeah. What does your mom cook when someone has a cold?

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.270
When someone has a cold?

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.610
Here you go, Kirin!

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.190
A tasty parsley salad!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.200
<i>For real?</i>

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.620
Just a ton of greens.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:57.410
Greens?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.330
It's all fresh... and refreshing...

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.250
That sounds wonderful.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.460
Uh, not really.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:13.550
I usually argue with Mom a lot,
but she's nice to me when I'm sick.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:16.260
Oh yeah, she bought me green tea pudding after that!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.840
That's green too...

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:21.010
You sound like you really love your Mom.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:23.980
Well...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.350
L-Love her?

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:29.360
Well, I mean, I don't <i>hate</i> her... so I suppose I like her, but...

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.820
What about you, Ryo?

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.690
You keep mentioning your Grandma,

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.990
but it looks like you've been
living alone for a while.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:42.080
Oh, Akira must not have told you.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.250
Ryo?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:49.170
I always lived with Grandma,
but she passed away a year ago.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.050
My parents are working overseas.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:59.640
Aunt Akira visits sometimes,
but she's really busy with work.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.180
Oh, I see...

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:05.060
That's why I'm glad you're here!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.850
I haven't had the opportunity to cook like this in a long time.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.400
Anyway, you should get some rest.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.320
You must have sweat a lot last night.
Let me change your sheets first.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.780
Goodni—

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:22.240
Kirin?

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.330
How about me?

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:30.170
Food's never as tasty when you eat alone.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.050
Alone?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:37.630
Dinner's something you should enjoy with someone important to you.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.800
If you don't have anyone, then maybe I can...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.390
Maybe I can be your family!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:45.640
Kirin...

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.270
Call me whatever you want!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.690
I'll be whoever you need!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.940
A father, a mother, a brother or sister, anything!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.530
What about a husband, or a wife?

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.320
Sure thing!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.450
How about a child?

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.450
Nope, not that.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:10.040
Have you finished your homework, Kirin?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.670
I'm just teasing.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.090
I said no!

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.460
Don't just—

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:22.720
There, there, I'll tuck you in.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:26.930
Ryo...

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.320
I gotta pee.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.110
Huh, Ryo?

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.280
You're gonna catch a cold too.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.710
Time to check out the leftovers.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.930
She read me like a book.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.800
<i>Eating too much is bad for your stomach.</i>

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.310
<i>Save it for when you feel better.</i>

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.490
Grandma...

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.490
Mom...

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.170
Kirin...

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.300
Ryo, I'm gonna get better,

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:45.220
and then I'm going to go make up with Mom.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.260
Good...

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:59.070
I feel great!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.730
You shouldn't run!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.610
I'll miss my train if I don't!

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.160
I'll make it back in time for lunch if I go straight to school!

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:08.160
Lunch?

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.040
Here, I've got a gift for you!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.330
Whoa!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.210
Thanks! See you next week!

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:23.090
Yeah, see you next week!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.010
I wonder what she gave me.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.480
Inari sushi!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:39.940
<i>Make this for your parents.</i>

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:45.530
<i>Hot pot tastes best when eaten with someone you love. From Ryo.</i>

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:55.410
<i>Grandma, Kirin showed me that I haven't gotten bad at cooking.</i>

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:59.630
<i>Meals eaten together taste great.</i>

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.340
<i>It's a very warm feeling.</i>

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:05.880
See you next week.

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:44.980
There's something you absolutely have to try at festivals.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:50.110
The fresh smell of the sea and the savory aroma of the sauce blend so well.

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:53.950
The arms and the legs have different textures.

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:57.950
The arms are all gummy,
and the legs are all chewy!

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:01.670
Either way, you like the tentacles, don't you?

00:24:01.670 --> 00:24:03.210
Yes! They're ten-tacular!

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:06.500
Next time, on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:08.510
"Fluffy and Crunchy".
